{
  "id": 4108,
  "title": "Borrow One Dollar",
  "russian_title": "О́н взя́л до́ллар в долг",
  "level": "Intermediate",
  "torfl_level": "A2",
  "hsk_tags": [
    "A2"
  ],
  "slug": "borrow-one-dollar",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/4108_borrow-one-dollar.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "A man walked into a bank and said to the manager: \"Can I borrow money?\" The manager replied: \"Of course, as long as there is a guarantee, you can borrow as much as you want. As long as you pay 6% interest, we will return the guarantee to you after one year.\" The manager thought he would borrow a lot, but he said, \"I want to borrow a dollar.\" He took out a stack of notes worth $500,000 and said, \"Can these be used as guarantee?\"",
    "The manager asked strangely: \"You have so much money, why do you need to borrow a dollar?\"",
    "The man replied: \"This may sound strange, but actually I just want to deposit the note here as a guarantee, which is safe and cheap.\""
  ],
  "english_full": "A man walked into a bank and said to the manager: \"Can I borrow money?\" The manager replied: \"Of course, as long as there is a guarantee, you can borrow as much as you want. As long as you pay 6% interest, we will return the guarantee to you after one year.\" The manager thought he would borrow a lot, but he said, \"I want to borrow a dollar.\" He took out a stack of notes worth $500,000 and said, \"Can these be used as guarantee?\"\n\nThe manager asked strangely: \"You have so much money, why do you need to borrow a dollar?\"\n\nThe man replied: \"This may sound strange, but actually I just want to deposit the note here as a guarantee, which is safe and cheap.\"",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "О́дин му́ж вошёл в банк и ска́зал дире́ктору: \"Мо́жно ли мне взять в долг ба́бки?\" Дире́ктор ответи́л: \"Есте́ственно, е́сли то́лько есть пору́ка, вы мо́жете взять столько, сколько захотите. Е́сли вы будите пла́тить 6% проце́нтов, мы возвратим вам пору́ку по́сле оди́н го́да.\" Дире́ктор поду́мал, что он возьмёт мно́го, но он ска́зал: \"Я хо́чу взять до́ллар.\" Он вы́тащил ки́пу не́стов сто́имостью 500 000 до́лларов и ска́зал: \"Мо́жно ли испо́льзовать э́ти для пору́ки?\"",
    "Дире́ктор стра́нно спроси́л: \"У вас та́кое мно́го ба́бок, почему́ вам ну́жен до́ллар в долг?\"",
    "Мужчи́на ответи́л: \"Э́то может показа́ться стра́нным, но на самы́й де́ле я хоч́у просто за́лежить зна́к здесь как пору́ку, кото́рый будет в безопа́сности и недорого́й.\""
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Ódin múzh voshёл v bank i skázal diréktoru: \"Mózhno li mne vzyat' v dolg bábki?\" Diréktor otvetíl: \"Ēstéstvenno, ési tól'ko yest' porúka, vy mózhite vzyat' stolkó, skolkó zakhotite. Ési vy budite plátit' 6% protséntov, my vozvratím vam porúku poslé odin góda.\" Diréktor podúmal, chto on voz'myot mnógo, no on skázal: \"Ya khóchu vzyat' dóllar.\" On výtashchil kípu néstov stóimost'yu 500 000 dóllarov i skázal: \"Mózhno li ispólyzovat' éti dlya porúki?\"",
    "Diréktor stránno sprosíl: \"U vas tákoye mnógo bábok, pochemú vam núzhen dóllar v dolg?\"",
    "Muzhchína otvetíl: \"Éto mózhyet pokazat'sya stránnym, no na samíy déle ya khóchu prósto zálezhit' znák zdes' kak porúku, kotorýy budet v bezopásnnosti i nedorogóy.\""
  ],
